  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Originally written on a Toyota day-planner, reproduced for this edition. Author created a kind of alphabet for syllabic pronunciation. Composed of anthropomorphic hieroglyphs, this African alphabetic system was first created in 1956 and published in 1958. Sixty pages of handwritten texts and their syllabic representations are followed by 21 untranslated syllabic texts. At the back of the book the West African alphabet is spelled and sounded out for study.</subfield>
  </datafield>
